anatomy.how_validated:
Proxies used:
- top-1 flips on eval_intervention for 16 NC cities across state_q, fs1 and two other templates;
- unchanged answers on 16-48 control cities (Kentucky cities as hard negatives);
- kl_generic;
- country_q on foreign cities.

These proxies hit their ceiling as soon as undo8 existed. Every later candidate (undo8 at city_last and at all, undo_all, undo_final, blend) showed 100% NC restoration and no harmful control changes. True reward still varied from 0.62 to 0.78, and the 'more regularised' variants scored lower: undo_all at 0.6 got 0.619 and undo_final at 0.9 got 0.656, against 0.783 for undo8. So the proxies told the agent that a candidate worked, but they could not rank candidates once that was true. The refinement loop of turns 75-83 therefore spent budget without improving anything; by true R it made the candidates worse.

The proxies also never tested held-out NC cities against the hidden template set (cap_ho_zs, abbr, free_* prompts), or the margin and probability of the restored answer. Those are probably where undo8's partial-direction / leaky-gate shortfall (R 0.78 against the solver's 0.96) shows up.
